
########################################################################################################################
# VERNIER-27 -- FIRM THE K* NUMBER.  EXPLORATORY, NOT PRE-REGISTERED
########################################################################################################################
  arm P band 10.00-24.26 nHz, 10 bins of 1/T = 1.584 nHz; array 116 pulsars
  seeds at array SNR 12; Mc 10^8.5-10^9.5; gamma = 1.56 (corrected sky, audited counts)
  COMB_CAP 32 (V25 used 8); max_turn = 2K + 16 (V25 used 16)

  V25 Arm K DEFECT: BAND holds 10 bins and chain() placed one seed in
  bins b < n_seed, so K = 12 and K = 16 both placed TEN seeds and are the
  same cell. The V25 extrapolation to K* ~ 20-25 ran off a tail that had
  stopped moving for that reason. V25 results at K <= 10 are unaffected.

